      "key": {
        "uuid": "047fbda8_8a5ab9f4",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002484
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T06:27:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. A retryable completion code is logged as a warning now; the error is only logged for non-retryable codes or when the retries are exhausted.",
      "parentUuid": "3f45f0d3_4fbc8d2a",
      "revId": "55c003903960d2f8ece90803f968685370ef22f7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0a985dc_383d84ed",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002297
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:42:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the FD is too busy to reply in time consistently? In worst case scenario, we\u0027ll have the 3 retries from requester code due to delays, followed by the 3 retries here",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "55c003903960d2f8ece90803f968685370ef22f7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfafac4c_4e1f0a90",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002484
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T06:27:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This retry only runs when the FD actually replies with PLDM_ERROR or PLDM_ERROR_NOT_READY. A timeout after the requester\u0027s retries goes through the no-response path and does not schedule a retry here, so the two do not stack. At most 3 extra requests are sent here.",
      "parentUuid": "f0a985dc_383d84ed",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "55c003903960d2f8ece90803f968685370ef22f7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "916d87c8_e894ae5e",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002303
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T05:10:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A late error response can schedule a retry after removal. Can we prevent that?",
      "revId": "55c003903960d2f8ece90803f968685370ef22f7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7de497b2_800b7a2d",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002484
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T06:27:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. The retry state is created in discoverFDs() and erased in removeFDs(), and the retry path uses find(), so a late response after removal no longer schedules a retry.",
      "parentUuid": "916d87c8_e894ae5e",
      "revId": "55c003903960d2f8ece90803f968685370ef22f7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    }
